   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"ltr\">The error is saying it’s trying to create an object that is larger than the largest allowed object. It’s not feasible, with R/qtl, to do scantwo() with such a large number of markers.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">R/qtl has no code to take advantage of GPUs. </div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">karl</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">On Oct 30, 2019, at 1:11 AM, Elad Oren &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elad...@mail.huji.ac.il</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></blockquote></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">﻿</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Karl</div><div><br></div><div>I have a large set of BC mapping popution - 7700 markers across 1400 individuals<br></div><div><br></div><div>Even when running 1 permutation I get the following error:<br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#606\">Error</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> calc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pairprob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">subset</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cross</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> chr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> thechr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> stp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> oe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> err</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#008\">long</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> vectors </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">argument </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> are </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> supported </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">C</span></div></code></div><br><div>This does not happen when using &quot;mr&quot; method. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Also is there a way I can run the permutations on a GPU to speed things up?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Elad<br></div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div>"
