   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div dir=\"ltr\">In principle, but that’s not going to get you around the problem.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">You need software that doesn’t try to store the full results. </div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">If scantwo works with method=“mr”, maybe it works when you have run calc.genoprob with step=0, so just calculating things at the markers and not adding intervening pseudomarkers.</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">karl</div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br><blockquote type=\"cite\">On Oct 30, 2019, at 5:56 AM, Elad Oren &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">elad...@mail.huji.ac.il</a>&gt; wrote:<br><br></blockquote></div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\">﻿</div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
